Deployment Documentation
Project Overview
This project demonstrates the deployment of a Dockerized microservice into a Kubernetes cluster using Deployments, Services, Ingress, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and Horizontal Pod Autoscaling (HPA).
Deployment Steps

1. Create Namespace
   kubectl apply -f namespace.yaml

2. Apply ConfigMap and Secret
   kubectl apply -f configmap.yaml
   kubectl apply -f secret.yaml

3. Deploy Application
   kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

4. Create Service
   kubectl apply -f service.yaml

5. Configure Autoscaling
   kubectl apply -f hpa.yaml

6. Configure Ingress
   kubectl apply -f ingress.yaml

Verification Commands

kubectl get pods -n week12-microservices
kubectl get deployments -n week12-microservices
kubectl get svc -n week12-microservices
kubectl get ingress -n week12-microservices
kubectl get hpa -n week12-microservices

Rolling Update

kubectl set image deployment/week12-microservice week12-microservice=week12-microservice:v2

kubectl rollout status deployment/week12-microservice

Rollback Procedure

kubectl rollout undo deployment/week12-microservice

Expected Outcome
A stable and scalable Kubernetes environment with multiple application replicas, service discovery, ingress routing, autoscaling, rolling updates, and rollback support.
